message: "If you use this model, its code, or its datasets, please cite it as below. Underlying publisher data carry their own citation requirements; see REFERENCES.md."
title: "The Primacy Premium: conditional forecasts of defense and commercial markets under Chinese military primacy, 2026 to 2035"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Agard
    given-names: Alyssa
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-29"
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
keywords:
  - defense economics
  - defense policy
  - conditional forecasting
  - uncertainty propagation
  - reserve currencies
  - arms transfers
  - military expenditure
  - reproducible research
abstract: >-
  A seeded, fully reproducible Python pipeline that models three pathways to
  Chinese military primacy by 2035 (accretion, retrenchment, demonstration)
  and tests whether the pathway conditions defense and commercial market
  outcomes more strongly than the endpoint itself. Sixteen scripts over
  fourteen source families produce thirty registered artifacts, three tested
  hypotheses with verdicts written by the pipeline, a unified hypothesis
  dataset, and an interactive results page.
